Track 3: Second-Hand Shrapnel
- Story & Context: The final stage of the ritual occurs in the ruins of an ancient observatory where the band scatters fragments of brass and ivory across the cracked foundation to satisfy the demands of the waning shadow. The local elders report that for three minutes, no one could walk straight, as the gravity shifted into a 432Hz hum that felt like being lifted by an invisible, humming hand. As the sun returns, the sound dissipates into a single, ringing bell note that lasts until the end of the day. "Everything that ticks must learn to stop."
